.TH DS4-CTL 1 "August 2026" "ds4-ctl 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ds4-ctl \- Control utility for the ds4-translator daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ds4-ctl
[\fIcommand\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ds4-ctl
is the control interface for the \fBds4-translator\fR daemon. It communicates with the daemon via a Unix domain socket located at \fI/run/ds4-translator.sock\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Displays the current status of the daemon, including the physical controller event node, connection interface type, virtual emulation target type, and host client connection state.
.TP
.B set-type ds4
Changes the target virtual controller emulation type to a Sony DualShock 4.
.TP
.B set-type dualsense
Changes the target virtual controller emulation type to a Sony DualSense.
.TP
.B set-type none
Disables virtual controller emulation.
.TP
.B set-backend <ds4|dualsense> <uhid|functionfs>
Changes that controller type's virtual device backend. Takes effect immediately if that type is currently active, otherwise persists for the next time it's selected via set-type. Defaults: dualsense=uhid, ds4=functionfs (uhid is not reliably detected as a DS4 in some Wine/Proton titles; functionfs is).
.TP
.B set-name <ds4|dualsense> <name>
Overrides the controller name/product string reported to the OS for that controller type (max 63 bytes, no newlines). Takes effect immediately (recreating the virtual device, with a brief input interruption) if that type is currently active, otherwise persists for the next time it's selected via set-type. The vendor ID stays Sony's regardless, so some games/drivers that cross-check name against vendor ID may treat a custom name with suspicion.
.TP
.B set-name <ds4|dualsense> --reset
Restores the default Sony name for that controller type.
.TP
.B identify
Blinks the physical controller's light bar three times and pulses its heavy motor once, so you can tell which pad the daemon is holding.
.TP
.B led <r> <g> <b> <rumble-left> <rumble-right>
Sends a light bar colour and rumble levels (each 0-255) straight to the physical controller, to test them. Not a setting: the next output report from the emulated device overwrites it.
.TP
.B led --reset
Hands the light bar and motors straight back to the emulated device.
.TP
.B test
Live-monitors the active controller: button, stick, touchpad and motion state, the physical controller's report rate and the delay the daemon adds, plus a log of the LED/rumble commands sent to it.
.TP
.B help
Shows basic usage and command synopsis.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/ds4-translator.sock
The Unix domain socket used to communicate with the daemon.
.TP
.I /etc/ds4-translator.conf
The translator configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ds4-translator (1)
